{# PROBLEMS WITH TRADITIONAL APPROACH #}
<section class="section section-light">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-split">
      <div class="content-text">
        <h2>Why the Traditional Approach Fails</h2>
        <p>The traditional dental lifecycle is designed to fail because it doesn't address the root causes of dental problems:</p>
        
        <div class="problem-list">
          <div class="problem-item">
            <h4>All Crowns Eventually Leak</h4>
            <p>No crown can seal perfectly. Bacteria inevitably gets underneath, creating an environment impossible to clean.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="problem-item">
            <h4>Each Step Weakens the Tooth</h4>
            <p>Every traditional treatment removes more healthy tooth structure, making the tooth progressively weaker.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="problem-item">
            <h4>Root Canals Don't Last</h4>
            <p>Root canals make teeth brittle and prone to fracture. Most root canal teeth are eventually lost.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="problem-item">
            <h4>It's Profitable to Fail</h4>
            <p>Traditional dentistry makes more money when treatments fail and need replacement. There's little incentive for long-term solutions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      
      <div class="content-image">
